WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.498
Wegener had evidence for continental drift but lacked a convincing driving

00:00:04.498 --> 00:00:08.646
mechanism. At a mid-ocean ridge, new basalt records magnetic polarity as

00:00:08.646 --> 00:00:12.793
it cools. Older bands move outward and keep their original polarity.

00:00:12.793 --> 00:00:16.564
Matching stripes on both sides are evidence for seafloor spreading.

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:25.206
Away from the ridge, oceanic lithosphere becomes older, cooler, denser, and

00:00:25.206 --> 00:00:30.062
thicker. Keep the layers separate: mantle lithosphere thickens as it cools,

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:34.476
sediment accumulates above, and crust stays roughly similar in thickness.
